  "page1": {
    "title": "The Magic of the Stage",
    "subtitle": "A play comes alive with a script, actors, a stage, and you.",
    "body": "Have you ever seen a play? A play tells a story on a stage. It needs a few important parts.\n\nFirst, the play needs a script. A script is the written words. It tells the actors what to say.\n\nNext, the play needs actors. The actors play the people in the story. They use voice and body to show feelings. A sad actor may speak in a low voice. A happy actor may jump and smile.\n\nThe play also needs a stage. The stage is the place for the show. Last, the play needs people to watch. These people are the audience.\n\nWhen the actors and the audience <mark>come together</mark>, the stage feels like magic.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/20.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Actors on a bright stage, a script in hand, and an audience watching together."
  },
